1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,540
On the night of November 5,

2
00:00:01,820 --> 00:00:03,500
1605, a man

3
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:05,060
and barrels of gunpowder

4
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:05,741
were discovered

5
00:00:05,781 --> 00:00:07,121
beneath the House of Lords

6
00:00:07,201 --> 00:00:07,701
in London.

7
00:00:08,101 --> 00:00:08,701
The man gave

8
00:00:08,741 --> 00:00:10,481
his name as John Johnson.

9
00:00:10,881 --> 00:00:11,341
His real

10
00:00:11,381 --> 00:00:12,941
name was Guy Fawkes.

11
00:00:13,541 --> 00:00:14,381
That same day,

12
00:00:14,621 --> 00:00:15,681
King James the First

13
00:00:15,721 --> 00:00:17,182
of England was due to attend

14
00:00:17,242 --> 00:00:18,382
the opening of Parliament.

15
00:00:18,802 --> 00:00:20,062
Members of both Houses

16
00:00:20,122 --> 00:00:20,762
would be gathered

17
00:00:20,802 --> 00:00:21,382
there with him.

18
00:00:21,762 --> 00:00:22,802
The people who had hidden

19
00:00:22,842 --> 00:00:23,942
the gunpowder planned

20
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:24,582
to kill them

21
00:00:24,802 --> 00:00:26,382
all in a single explosion.

22
00:00:26,782 --> 00:00:27,443
But Fawkes

23
00:00:27,583 --> 00:00:29,103
was not the leader of the plot.

24
00:00:29,463 --> 00:00:31,043
And yet, centuries later,

25
00:00:31,343 --> 00:00:33,063
it is his name that millions

26
00:00:33,103 --> 00:00:34,503
of people still remember.

27
00:00:35,023 --> 00:00:35,983
Two years earlier,

28
00:00:36,283 --> 00:00:37,623
England had a new monarch.

29
00:00:38,024 --> 00:00:39,204
Many English Catholics

30
00:00:39,304 --> 00:00:40,724
hoped that James would ease

31
00:00:40,764 --> 00:00:41,264
the religious

32
00:00:41,324 --> 00:00:42,444
restrictions imposed

33
00:00:42,524 --> 00:00:43,524
under his predecessor,

34
00:00:43,724 --> 00:00:44,664
Elizabeth the First.

35
00:00:45,064 --> 00:00:46,364
Catholics faced fines

36
00:00:46,464 --> 00:00:47,324
and persecution,

37
00:00:47,544 --> 00:00:48,544
and Catholic priests

38
00:00:48,665 --> 00:00:49,805
were being hunted down.

39
00:00:50,225 --> 00:00:51,465
Those hopes for change

40
00:00:51,605 --> 00:00:52,465
were disappointed.

41
00:00:52,885 --> 00:00:54,745
So a small group of Catholics

42
00:00:54,805 --> 00:00:56,305
decided to take action.

43
00:00:56,665 --> 00:00:57,645
They did not represent

44
00:00:57,905 --> 00:00:58,945
all English Catholics.

45
00:00:59,345 --> 00:01:00,586
The plot was a decision

46
00:01:00,626 --> 00:01:02,386
made by specific individuals.

47
00:01:02,826 --> 00:01:03,626
The group was led

48
00:01:03,706 --> 00:01:04,446
by a nobleman

49
00:01:04,526 --> 00:01:05,686
named Robert Catesby.

50
00:01:06,066 --> 00:01:07,286
His plan was to blow

51
00:01:07,346 --> 00:01:07,926
up Parliament

52
00:01:07,986 --> 00:01:08,786
during its opening

53
00:01:08,846 --> 00:01:10,547
ceremony and kill the king.

54
00:01:11,027 --> 00:01:12,467
Guy Fawkes also joined

55
00:01:12,487 --> 00:01:13,227
the conspiracy.

56
00:01:13,587 --> 00:01:14,447
He was a soldier

57
00:01:14,507 --> 00:01:15,107
who had served

58
00:01:15,147 --> 00:01:16,147
in the Spanish army.

59
00:01:16,487 --> 00:01:17,627
His job was to guard

60
00:01:17,667 --> 00:01:18,827
the gunpowder and,

61
00:01:19,027 --> 00:01:20,807
when the time came, ignite it.

62
00:01:21,168 --> 00:01:22,108
But the explosion

63
00:01:22,168 --> 00:01:23,368
was only the beginning

64
00:01:23,408 --> 00:01:24,048
of their plan.

65
00:01:24,408 --> 00:01:25,468
The conspirators hoped

66
00:01:25,508 --> 00:01:26,648
to launch an uprising

67
00:01:26,748 --> 00:01:28,068
and seize the king's young

68
00:01:28,128 --> 00:01:29,528
daughter, Princess Elizabeth.

69
00:01:29,948 --> 00:01:30,568
They believed

70
00:01:30,608 --> 00:01:32,029
that once James was dead,

71
00:01:32,269 --> 00:01:32,789
they could bring

72
00:01:32,849 --> 00:01:34,769
about changes in the country.

73
00:01:34,949 --> 00:01:36,829
In 1605, the conspirators

74
00:01:36,929 --> 00:01:37,649
rented a space

75
00:01:37,709 --> 00:01:38,449
beneath the House

76
00:01:38,489 --> 00:01:39,529
of Lords and brought

77
00:01:39,569 --> 00:01:40,829
the gunpowder inside.

78
00:01:41,189 --> 00:01:42,309
The opening of Parliament

79
00:01:42,349 --> 00:01:43,670
had been postponed several

80
00:01:43,730 --> 00:01:45,190
times, but it was finally

81
00:01:45,250 --> 00:01:46,690
scheduled for November 5.

82
00:01:47,210 --> 00:01:48,470
Everything seemed ready.

83
00:01:48,930 --> 00:01:50,470
Then a letter appeared.

84
00:01:50,870 --> 00:01:51,690
On October 26,

85
00:01:52,370 --> 00:01:53,230
Lord Monteagle

86
00:01:53,290 --> 00:01:54,391
received an anonymous

87
00:01:54,451 --> 00:01:55,691
warning advising him

88
00:01:55,851 --> 00:01:57,091
not to attend Parliament.

89
00:01:57,451 --> 00:01:58,251
The letter reached

90
00:01:58,291 --> 00:01:59,231
the royal authorities.

91
00:01:59,691 --> 00:02:00,171
Who sent

92
00:02:00,211 --> 00:02:01,571
it remains unknown.

93
00:02:02,031 --> 00:02:02,911
Suspicion fell

94
00:02:02,991 --> 00:02:04,171
on one of the conspirators,

95
00:02:04,452 --> 00:02:05,672
a relative of Monteagle,

96
00:02:05,932 --> 00:02:06,912
but his authorship

97
00:02:06,992 --> 00:02:07,912
was never proven.

98
00:02:08,292 --> 00:02:09,112
The conspirators

99
00:02:09,212 --> 00:02:10,152
learned about the letter.

100
00:02:10,572 --> 00:02:11,652
Now there was a danger

101
00:02:11,692 --> 00:02:12,472
that the authorities

102
00:02:12,512 --> 00:02:13,532
would search the building

103
00:02:13,652 --> 00:02:14,952
and discover the gunpowder.

104
00:02:15,393 --> 00:02:15,973
Even so,

105
00:02:16,233 --> 00:02:17,633
they decided to go ahead.

106
00:02:18,053 --> 00:02:18,473
On the night

107
00:02:18,533 --> 00:02:19,713
before Parliament was due

108
00:02:19,753 --> 00:02:21,073
to open, the authorities

109
00:02:21,153 --> 00:02:22,053
conducted a search.

110
00:02:22,413 --> 00:02:23,413
They found Fawkes

111
00:02:23,493 --> 00:02:24,053
near the room

112
00:02:24,113 --> 00:02:25,253
containing the gunpowder

113
00:02:25,453 --> 00:02:26,234
and arrested him.

114
00:02:26,614 --> 00:02:27,414
The explosion

115
00:02:27,794 --> 00:02:28,494
never happened.

116
00:02:28,734 --> 00:02:29,374
While Fawkes

117
00:02:29,434 --> 00:02:30,354
was being questioned

118
00:02:30,414 --> 00:02:31,654
in London, Catesby

119
00:02:31,714 --> 00:02:33,214
and other conspirators tried

120
00:02:33,254 --> 00:02:34,274
to gather supporters

121
00:02:34,394 --> 00:02:35,374
outside the capital.

122
00:02:35,694 --> 00:02:36,294
But the large

123
00:02:36,394 --> 00:02:37,455
uprising they had hoped

124
00:02:37,515 --> 00:02:39,195
for never materialized.

125
00:02:39,675 --> 00:02:40,155
A few days

126
00:02:40,215 --> 00:02:41,415
later, the authorities

127
00:02:41,515 --> 00:02:42,675
caught up with the fugitives.

128
00:02:43,095 --> 00:02:44,215
Catesby was killed

129
00:02:44,255 --> 00:02:44,855
in a shootout.

130
00:02:45,315 --> 00:02:46,475
Fawkes was imprisoned

131
00:02:46,515 --> 00:02:47,035
in the Tower

132
00:02:47,075 --> 00:02:48,576
of London and interrogated.

133
00:02:48,996 --> 00:02:50,576
A royal order has survived

134
00:02:50,836 --> 00:02:52,496
authorizing the use of torture

135
00:02:52,536 --> 00:02:53,056
against him.

136
00:02:53,516 --> 00:02:55,876
In January 1606, Fawkes

137
00:02:55,996 --> 00:02:56,936
and the other surviving

138
00:02:56,976 --> 00:02:58,657
conspirators were executed.

139
00:02:59,077 --> 00:03:00,337
The conspirators had wanted

140
00:03:00,377 --> 00:03:01,517
to change the position

141
00:03:01,537 --> 00:03:02,557
of English Catholics.

142
00:03:02,897 --> 00:03:03,677
But after the plot

143
00:03:03,777 --> 00:03:04,977
failed, suspicion

144
00:03:05,017 --> 00:03:06,737
toward Catholics intensified,

145
00:03:06,957 --> 00:03:07,737
and the authorities

146
00:03:07,837 --> 00:03:08,597
introduced new

147
00:03:08,657 --> 00:03:09,898
requirements for their oath

148
00:03:09,938 --> 00:03:10,498
of allegiance.

149
00:03:11,018 --> 00:03:12,318
November 5 itself

150
00:03:12,438 --> 00:03:13,998
became a day of thanksgiving

151
00:03:14,078 --> 00:03:14,858
for the survival

152
00:03:14,878 --> 00:03:16,158
of the king and Parliament.

153
00:03:16,598 --> 00:03:17,198
Over time,

154
00:03:17,438 --> 00:03:18,378
a tradition developed

155
00:03:18,438 --> 00:03:19,818
in Britain of marking the day

156
00:03:19,858 --> 00:03:21,639
with bonfires and fireworks.

157
00:03:22,039 --> 00:03:23,039
People began burning

158
00:03:23,199 --> 00:03:24,519
effigies of Guy Fawkes

159
00:03:24,699 --> 00:03:25,679
on those bonfires.

160
00:03:26,099 --> 00:03:27,219
And so a man

161
00:03:27,259 --> 00:03:28,119
who had never led

162
00:03:28,159 --> 00:03:29,979
the conspiracy gave his name

163
00:03:30,039 --> 00:03:31,020
to a celebration

164
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:31,920
that commemorates

165
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:32,720
its failure.
